Map data
--------
Street and speed-camera data: © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the
Open Database License (ODbL), https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

- The streets around the route come from vector tiles generated from
  OpenStreetMap by VersaTiles (tiles.versatiles.org, Shortbread schema), with
  the Overpass API as the fallback.
- The companion also has a reader for OpenMapTiles-schema tiles from OpenFreeMap
  (tiles.openfreemap.org); it is not enabled today. Tiles from that source are
  "OpenFreeMap © OpenMapTiles. Data from OpenStreetMap." https://openmaptiles.org/
- The hosted VersaTiles "osm" tileset is merged with land cover:
  © ESA WorldCover project 2021 / Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data
  (2021) processed by ESA WorldCover consortium. (CC BY 4.0)
- Speed cameras come from OpenStreetMap (highway=speed_camera) through the
  Overpass API.
- Address search uses Photon (photon.komoot.io), which serves OpenStreetMap data.
- tools/fixtures/corridor_*.json and tools/fixtures/overpass_radars_*.json are
  recorded Overpass responses with OpenStreetMap data (ODbL).
- tools/fixtures/route_*.json are recorded OSRM responses
  (https://routing.openstreetmap.de, run by FOSSGIS), with OpenStreetMap data
  (ODbL).

Official speed cameras missing from OpenStreetMap: pardal
(https://github.com/Murkiriel/pardal), under the ODbL 1.0, a database derived
from OpenStreetMap and from official open data. The app downloads
brasil/radares.csv and uses only fixed, active cameras with a direction. The
pardal sources, with the license its README gives each one:
- City of São Paulo (GeoSampa, CET-SP): the city's active cameras, with speed
  limit and direction. Municipal open data; CET's "Fiscalização Eletrônica do
  Trânsito" dataset on the city's open data portal
  (https://dados.prefeitura.sp.gov.br) is CC BY.
- ANTT (cameras and signage on federal concessions): CC BY.
- City of Rio de Janeiro (IPP, SMTR/CET-Rio): CC BY 4.0.
- BHTrans (Belo Horizonte): CC BY.
- Inmetro (PSIE, speed meters): Creative Commons.
- DNIT (PNCV, SNV and ICM), PRF (mobile radar segments, violations and
  crashes), DER-SP / Artesp, DER-GO (Goinfra), DER-PE, DER-MG, IDE-Sisema
  (SEMAD-MG), SIE-SC, IBGE (meshes and CNEFE), Detran-DF, and the cities of
  Fortaleza, Recife, João Pessoa and Curitiba: government open data.
- EPTC (Porto Alegre): municipal open data.
- PRF (spreadsheet of fixed cameras on concessions): no written license.

Routing
-------
Directions powered by Mapbox (Mapbox Directions API, plus Mapbox geocoding as an
alternative to Photon). Each user brings their own Mapbox access token, typed
into the companion app; no token ships in this repository or in the APK, and
each user is responsible for complying with the Mapbox Terms of Service.
